{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism","id":1264948,"title":"Scion and Monotheism","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-06T06:44:46-08:00","id":1264948,"title":"Scion and Monotheism","content":"Likely this has come up before and I apologies if I have not found the answer, but something that has bugged me is that Scion take creatives licence with polytheistic religions, but there is no real mention or comment on monotheistic religions. From my perspective if we have a game about mythic figures and godly beings that all faiths would be represented in some form and fashion. Was this done because the writers and the company didn't want to offend a large chunk of the religious community, highlight religions that do not get a in-depth spot light, or some other reason?<br /> <br /> I don't ask out of malice and am honestly curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T09:55:21-08:00","id":1264998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism#post1264948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likely this has come up before and I apologies if I have not found the answer, but something that has bugged me is that Scion take creatives licence with polytheistic religions, but there is no real mention or comment on monotheistic religions. From my perspective if we have a game about mythic figures and godly beings that all faiths would be represented in some form and fashion. Was this done because the writers and the company didn't want to offend a large chunk of the religious community, highlight religions that do not get a in-depth spot light, or some other reason?<br /> <br /> I don't ask out of malice and am honestly curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a sidebar in Hero on Page 24 that discusses Monotheism. In addition, the game contains the Orisha, who are explicitly a monotheistic Pantheon and mentioned as such in their write-up, and also the Deva, many of whose followers (myself included) are monotheistic. So monotheism is very much there in the book. Though I will note that, given the number of religious beliefs that Humanity has espoused over the ages, it is impossible to represent them all, no matter in what form or fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 11-06-2018, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T10:06:32-08:00","id":1265002,"title":"","content":"OK, thank you for that. I had missed that sidebar. I will read over it and give it some thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T11:13:20-08:00","id":1265019,"title":"","content":"*Awaits the inevitable Henotheism rant*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T12:37:21-08:00","id":1265068,"title":"","content":"In addition, I know that Neall has said he doesn't want anybody to feel like they picked the 'wrong religion' when reading Scion.<br /> <br /> At my table, my stance is &quot;The Abrahamic religions are as true as any other religion in the World. However, we aren't touching that with a ten foot pole.&quot; Because people have tried before, tried to make various Angelic/Abrahamic/YHWH Pantheon Writeups... And most of them go &quot;Okay this is a fucking minefield and there's actually a LOT of stuff to untangle so I'm out&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think the team want to do a Caananite Pantheon in Demigod, which will probably address the elephant in the room.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T13:32:45-08:00","id":1265106,"title":"","content":"In terms of risk of offending people - I don\u2019t see any difference from using Hinduism in a game. Except of course that the writers and publishers are largely of Abrahamic background themselves so it should be MORE ok.<br /> <br /> For the \u201cmonotheism doesn\u2019t cosmologically mix with a polytheistic setting\u201d arguments, that isn\u2019t preventing the Yazata from placing their one true God as a Primordial, and Zoroastrianism\u2019s angelic beings as God-level.<br /> <br /> All the hand wringing seems hypocritical to me in that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-06-2018, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T07:32:59-08:00","id":1265272,"title":"","content":"Mainly just lean into the idea that Primordials are BIG and no one is really sure where one begins and another ends.<br /> <br /> COULD The Three Pure Ones = Amenominakanushi/Takamimusuhi/Kamimusuhi = Olorun/Oludomare/Olofin = the Holy Trinity = the trimurti faces of Brahman and/or the tridevi faces of Shakti?<br /> <br /> The Orisha are open to the idea, but more broadly, who knows?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T21:56:31-08:00","id":1266094,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, Scion 2e is better equipped to handle monotheism than 1e was. 1e didn't have Primordials or Chosen Scions, two concepts that are essential to monotheistic factions in 2e, the first allowing a Pantheon to have a \u201cHighest God\u201d and the second allowing it to have Scions who aren't literal children of the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T15:03:39-08:00","id":1268999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1265068#post1265068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, I know that Neall has said he doesn't want anybody to feel like they picked the 'wrong religion' when reading Scion.<br /> <br /> At my table, my stance is &quot;The Abrahamic religions are as true as any other religion in the World. However, we aren't touching that with a ten foot pole.&quot; Because people have tried before, tried to make various Angelic/Abrahamic/YHWH Pantheon Writeups... And most of them go &quot;Okay this is a fucking minefield and there's actually a LOT of stuff to untangle so I'm out&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think the team want to do a Caananite Pantheon in Demigod, which will probably address the elephant in the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tend to look at them as being almost entirely hands off about the World in the modern day for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T00:46:06-08:00","id":1270041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1268999#post1268999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I tend to look at them as being almost entirely hands off about the World in the modern day for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, no moreso than the other Pantheons. I've no doubt that in the World there ARE Scions who claim that their power comes from YHWH, or one of His servants.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262836-the-tzevaot-the-heavenly-host-the-abrahamic-pantheon\">I'll take this moment to link another user's very well-made homebrew Angelic Host Pantheon</a>, which has a sidebar noting that the Angels definitely exist, and they say that the Creator does as well, but that the Angels mostly seem to refuse to provide any clarification for the smaller questions about the cosmological breakdown.<br /> <br /> Such as &quot;So was Jesus actually the Son of God?&quot;, with the reason being &quot;Each time we provide clarification you mortals make even more splinter groups. Now take this sword and go kill some demons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T01:02:20-08:00","id":1270043,"title":"","content":"Definitely moreso than other pantheons. I'd rather just not use them for anything.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about my take, not the game's take. I'm not sure the game has a take, tbh.<br /> <br /> I also don't really like the whole &quot;angels have scions&quot; thing, tbh. In my own games, only actual gods would have them. I also have a lot of issues with combining Christianity, Judaism, and Islam into a singular &quot;pantheon.&quot; Anyway, I'm not advising anyone else on what to do or not to do, just what I prefer to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-23-2018, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T01:15:41-08:00","id":1270047,"title":"","content":"It's a weird objection, possibly, but the one thing that made me hold back really getting into Scion was the lack of Judeo-Christian representation. Not that I'm particularly religious, and the various other pantheons were interesting (I have the PDFs as a Kickstarter backer), but I'd like to see all the religions represented. They may be monotheistic, but there is a whole pantheon of angels (and demons) to flesh out instead, and it would be a good inclusion for me. I know it's not hapenning any time soon though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T02:49:51-08:00","id":1270064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270043#post1270043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't really like the whole &quot;angels have scions&quot; thing, tbh. In my own games, only actual gods would have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you define a God? The Orisha would say they're not Gods if you asked them. They'd say they have One Big True God, they're just like messengers of them.<br /> <br /> Not unlike Angels, when you think about it.<br /> <br /> And most Angels in a hypothetical Abrahamic Angelic Host Pantheon would probably, A, have Chosen Scions... And B would insist that the Scions are Chosen in Accordance with the Will of the Divine, of which they are but mere messengers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T05:59:07-08:00","id":1270094,"title":"","content":"As an Abrahamic Monotheist in one of the branches that often gets told &quot;you're not really monotheist&quot; (aka Catholicism), I'd note that there is no talk about the Abrahamics being combined into a single pantheon as far as I know. Even in terms of home-brewing some Christianity, I was thinking in terms of at least the Angelic Choir and the Catholic Saints being separate pantheons. I can't speak to how the Islamic or Judaic pantheons would work out. But with significant cultural differences they'd be separate.<br /> <br /> And they'd certainly be more about the Chosen Scions than anything else, born scions from the Angelic Choir would be in for a bad time since Nephilim are considered bad news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T10:57:29-08:00","id":1270145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270094#post1270094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Abrahamic Monotheist in one of the branches that often gets told &quot;you're not really monotheist&quot; (aka Catholicism), I'd note that there is no talk about the Abrahamics being combined into a single pantheon as far as I know. Even in terms of home-brewing some Christianity, I was thinking in terms of at least the Angelic Choir and the Catholic Saints being separate pantheons. I can't speak to how the Islamic or Judaic pantheons would work out. But with significant cultural differences they'd be separate.<br /> <br /> And they'd certainly be more about the Chosen Scions than anything else, born scions from the Angelic Choir would be in for a bad time since Nephilim are considered bad news.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are cultural and (HUGE!) theological differences, but remember that Scion is about Myth, not Religion (hence the Roman Pantheon being Mantles of the Greek, despite their religious differences, because their mythic NARRATIVE is a direct extension of the Greek).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T11:14:39-08:00","id":1270150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270043#post1270043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely moreso than other pantheons. I'd rather just not use them for anything.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about my take, not the game's take. I'm not sure the game has a take, tbh.<br /> <br /> I also don't really like the whole &quot;angels have scions&quot; thing, tbh. In my own games, only actual gods would have them. I also have a lot of issues with combining Christianity, Judaism, and Islam into a singular &quot;pantheon.&quot; Anyway, I'm not advising anyone else on what to do or not to do, just what I prefer to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) if the high Legend agents of a Primordials One True God can\u2019t have Scions you need to drop the Orisha and the Yazata in their entireties.<br /> <br /> 2) As I said above, while the Abrahamic faiths are very different, they share a mythic narrative foundation (used here in the original meaning of \u201cmyth\u201d, not meant to mean \u201cfalse\u201d) which is what Pantheons are based on.<br /> <br /> (I mean if Shaktism, Shaivism, Vaishnavaism, Hari Krishnas, Smartism, and pre-Puranic Vedism can all share one Pantheon...)<br /> <br /> The contradictions that arise out of this are why Mantles exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-23-2018, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T13:25:09-08:00","id":1270185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270064#post1270064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you define a God? The Orisha would say they're not Gods if you asked them. They'd say they have One Big True God, they're just like messengers of them.<br /> <br /> Not unlike Angels, when you think about it.<br /> <br /> And most Angels in a hypothetical Abrahamic Angelic Host Pantheon would probably, A, have Chosen Scions... And B would insist that the Scions are Chosen in Accordance with the Will of the Divine, of which they are but mere messengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orisha are Yoruban deities, though. They can be emissaries of Olodumare and gods in their own right, and most pantheons have a ruler who may also be supreme.<br /> <br /> &quot;How would you define a god&quot; is a pretty huge question, and I'm not even going to try to answer it. I'm just going to say that Yoruban Orisha <i>are</i> gods, however they're presented in Scion, and angels are <i>not</i>.<br /> <br /> And Thrythlind makes a good point about combining Christianity, Judaism, and Islam, and their many sects into a single pantheon. That's definitely not something I'd be comfortable doing in an RPG.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T13:29:03-08:00","id":1270187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270150#post1270150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) if the high Legend agents of a Primordials One True God can\u2019t have Scions you need to drop the Orisha and the Yazata in their entireties.<br /> <br /> 2) As I said above, while the Abrahamic faiths are very different, they share a mythic narrative foundation (used here in the original meaning of \u201cmyth\u201d, not meant to mean \u201cfalse\u201d) which is what Pantheons are based on.<br /> <br /> (I mean if Shaktism, Shaivism, Vaishnavaism, Hari Krishnas, Smartism, and pre-Puranic Vedism can all share one Pantheon...)<br /> <br /> The contradictions that arise out of this are why Mantles exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This is completely irrelevant, because the Yoruban religion is not Christianity, and Olodumare does not occupy the same role as Jehovah. Olodumare occupies a *similarly described* role, but the Orisha are still described as deities in sources outside Scion whereas no serious scholar would ever describe angels as deities.<br /> <br /> 2) The three are also very different and collapsing them into one pantheon is probably worse than not using them at all.<br /> <br /> I'd appreciate it if people didn't get super invested in me not using someone else's house rules, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T13:59:32-08:00","id":1270189,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not invested in what you do at your table, I\u2019m discussing the arguments for what is consistently workable in the game.<br /> <br /> The Yazatas are also angelic servants of Ahura Mazda, the sole actual God in Zoroastrianism.<br /> <br /> Most of the Tuatha De Danann were never worshipped as gods. Nor was Loki. Trying to delineate which numinous high Legend being is and is not a \u201cgod\u201d seems more a matter of theology than Myth, which is emphatically not the point of Scion.<br /> <br /> The Abrahamic traditions are very different from each other (particularly Christianity being as heavily Hellenized as it is compared to the more purely Semitic theologies of Judaism and Islam - thanks Paul). So are the diverse religions that Europeans collectively labeled \u201cHinduism\u201d. The latter share a pantheon because of the shared mythic narrative of the Vedas*. Why would it be less accurate for the former to share a Pantheon because of the shared mythic narrative of Eden, Abraham, Exodus....<br /> <br /> <br /> *Note that despite a shared regional origin, Buddhism gets a separate Pantheon (even aside from individually Buddhist gods in other Pantheons like Guanshiyin and Hachiman) because it doesn't use the Vedas as its holy narrative, while that's the ultimate uniting thread for the diverse traditions that are still grouped together as &quot;Hinduism&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-23-2018, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T14:34:47-08:00","id":1270196,"title":"","content":"Go back and read my first post in this thread and ask whether I was trying to make general statements about what is consistently workable in the game vs. what I said that I specifically prefer to do myself? Why was I asked to justify this, to define what &quot;god&quot; means and in general challenged on what I personally want in my own game? I didn't reply telling anyone else what they should do.<br /> <br /> Invoking Loki and the Tuatha De Danann is also not relevant, because again these are not Christianity and those figures occupy the same space gods do whereas, again, angels do <i>not</i>. Also, Tuatha De apparently means &quot;people of the gods.&quot; Also also, it looks like they were worshipped, or at least Christian writers acknowledged they were worshipped but didn't believe they should be.<br /> <br /> As far as Zoroastrianism, it is true that Ahura Mazda is considered the supreme being, but the word &quot;yazata&quot; literally means &quot;worthy of worship or veneration.&quot; Which does not sound like they fill the same role as Christian angels. I don't know that it really works any better than Christianity would <i>in my opinion</i> but I also do not think it makes sense to put it in the same category of Christianity simply because they're both monotheistic and have supreme beings. And the yazatas, like the angels, are a house rule as far as I know and don't exist in any official Scion material.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, though, I don't care what other people do at their tables, and I couldn't possibly care less if other people use Abrahamic or Zoroastrian religions as the basis for pantheons in Scion. I, <i>personally,</i> do not want to use Christianity, Judaism, or Islam in <i>my personal</i> games for the reasons I have previously stated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-23-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T14:38:06-08:00","id":1270197,"title":"","content":"Yazatas are gonna be in the Scion Companion. They are definitely a thing in setting, they were mentioned a couple of times in Hero","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T14:41:48-08:00","id":1270198,"title":"","content":"This article about whether Loki was worshipped is interesting, and mentions that other Norse gods don't have any evidence of being worshipped. In each case, though, absence of evidence is not evidence of absence and I'd hesitate to claim that Loki was never worshipped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://polytheist.com/orgrandr-lokean/2014/12/02/evidence-of-lokis-worship/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://polytheist.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/09/dagulf_final_header.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://polytheist.com/orgrandr-lokean/2014/12/02/evidence-of-lokis-worship/\" target=\"_blank\"> Evidence of Loki's Worship? &ndash; Polytheist.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://polytheist.com/orgrandr-lokean/2014/12/02/evidence-of-lokis-worship/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://polytheist.com/orgrandr-lokean/2014/12/02/evidence-of-lokis-worship/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> One of the most pervasive (and unfounded) arguments against Loki&rsquo;s worship in American Heathenry, is that we have no physical or written evidence to suggest he was ever worshipped in the past. This has often been used as &ldquo;proof&rdquo; that he was reviled in Scandinavia, since he was seemingly so hated that nobody would want to worship Loki or name anything after him. However, there is a similar lack of evidence for the worship of&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T14:42:56-08:00","id":1270199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270197#post1270197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yazatas are gonna be in the Scion Companion. They are definitely a thing in setting, they were mentioned a couple of times in Hero</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. I still don't see them as basically angels, and I would hope that they're not presented that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T15:05:20-08:00","id":1270204,"title":"","content":"Well the thing is being worshipped, isn't really important in whether your gonna be in a pantheon or not. The reason why Glamourweaver brought up the TDD is that we know for a fact they weren't worshipped as Gods. It be weird if they did, because there sources after all were written by Christian monks. Now theres always the argument that they were worshipped before the coming of Christianity, but the problem is that we have literally no idea about the Irish Gods of Pre-Christianity. Everything and everything about them in Scion came from one place, and that was the medieval manuscripts written well past that point. Even their Creation myth has humans being their enemies then their worshippers, and is why they were often malicious towards them under a different name in myths, the Fair Folk. In any case that's just me making it clear what position the Tuatha held thou Watcher can probably explain it better. Since that is his major. <br /> <br /> As how this relate to the Arahamic faiths, well that depends. No one is objecting that If you don't want to play it like that you have to and that's fine anyhow, you do as you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T15:39:48-08:00","id":1270207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270196#post1270196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invoking Loki and the Tuatha De Danann is also not relevant, because again these are not Christianity and those figures occupy the same space gods do whereas, again, angels do <i>not</i>. Also, Tuatha De apparently means &quot;people of the gods.&quot; Also also, it looks like they were worshipped, or at least Christian writers acknowledged they were worshipped but didn't believe they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not particularly a fight I want to get involved in, but I will lean in since Iceblade mentioned it and just to prevent any misunderstandings. While T\u00faatha D\u00e9 does mean 'God Peoples' in Old Irish [though for this context I prefer t\u00faath as 'tribe'] we have zero evidence of any worship of any of the figures, and we can prove that several of them are made up well into the medieval period such as Ler. There is a very good book about this called Ireland's Immortals by Mark Williams, but I can give a quick breakdown.<br /> <br /> Essentially, when you think about it, it's nonsensical that all of Ireland would somehow have a unified Pantheon. A bunch of interwarring tribal factions semi-organized into small confederations constantly at each other's throats does not breed a unified religious system, same as what we see in Gaul. It appears (though our ability to say this is incredibly hazy) that each tribal group likely had its own collection of figures with maybe a small scant handful that crossed between tribal boundaries.<br /> <br /> Modern scholarship in Celtic Studies has abandoned the theory that the Irish Sagas are clearly representative of anything outside of the era they were being recorded in. The T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann and their stories are a Christian era-recreation of a 'Pagan' past (keep in mind the earliest sagas we have are from 200 years post Christianization where the latest are nearly 1,000 years post) which was based on a desire for local stories. Some of these stories may have had a basis, though a particularly dodgey one, in pre-Christian belief, but the vast majority of them are solidly not.<br /> <br /> The Saga authors almost never reference the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 as Gods even [Yes, Cormac's Glossary suggests it for one of the four Manann\u00e1ns and that one description of The Dagda suggest it but that's a whole different kettle of fish], not even as Gods who shouldn't be worshiped. The more popular explanations for them at the time of the sagas are either 'Unfallen Humans' (don't ask how that could have happened but it was one of their ideas), and 'Half-Fallen Angels' (Angels who were neutral during The War in Heaven and thus fall but not as far as the rebels). The idea that the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 might be worshiped never comes up in the sagas even, and the vast majority of their Cosmology is based on Biblical cosmology. The TDD can trace their ancestry back to Noah I believe using the geneology traditions in the Book of Invasions.<br /> <br /> So, Christian authors at the time never acknowledged that they were worshiped, and probably made about 90% of them up after the fact to make an 'appropriately pagan past' after it had mostly been obliterated. The word for 'God' being part of their name doesn't really suggest anything, C\u00faChulainn isn't a dog even though he has 'dog' in his name, it's that sort of thing. We don't even have any archeological evidence for worship of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T15:56:25-08:00","id":1270209,"title":"","content":"I just remembered, Anansi has a Scion in printed canon. While one can argue the Abosom are beings worthy of veneration even though beneath an omnipotent One True God, like the Orisha and Yazata, and unlike the Abrahamic angels who reject any worship in favor of absolute monotheism (Catholic and Orthodox veneration of Saints including Archangels really getting pushed out of the Abrahamic monotheism clubhouse by this narrow a distinction, FWIW, as would aspects of Sufism) - that does not include Anansi, who is not a true Abosom, but is rather a folk hero who serves the narrative function of a divinity through his \u201cJust So\u201d type stories. And he\u2019s by far the most popular figure of Ashanti myth!<br /> <br /> Again, Scion\u2019s about Myth, not Religion. Worship doesn\u2019t define a \u201cGod\u201d in this context, Legend does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-23-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T18:14:20-08:00","id":1270242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270185#post1270185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How would you define a god&quot; is a pretty huge question, and I'm not even going to try to answer it. I'm just going to say that Yoruban Orisha <i>are</i> gods, however they're presented in Scion, and angels are <i>not</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Orisha, as far as I know (which isn't much admittedly) would NOT say they are Gods. They are very powerful entities capable of great things, but they themselves would say that they're not Gods.<br /> <br /> No more than the Angels would say that they're Gods. They're simply very powerful beings that enact the Will of the Almighty. In Game terms, the mightiest of Angels would almost certainly be Gods <i>of a sort, </i>mechanically, regardless of what they themselves say. You're actually kind of presuming quite a bit here.<br /> <br /> Now again, your table, your rules, and nobody's going to kick down the door and force you to play this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-23-2018, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T18:56:17-08:00","id":1270245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270242#post1270242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Orisha, as far as I know (which isn't much admittedly) would NOT say they are Gods. They are very powerful entities capable of great things, but they themselves would say that they're not Gods.<br /> <br /> No more than the Angels would say that they're Gods. They're simply very powerful beings that enact the Will of the Almighty. In Game terms, the mightiest of Angels would almost certainly be Gods <i>of a sort, </i>mechanically, regardless of what they themselves say. You're actually kind of presuming quite a bit here.<br /> <br /> Now again, your table, your rules, and nobody's going to kick down the door and force you to play this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually has me curious, do we know anything of how old Yoruban worship was structured? I honestly don't know much about the theological stuff about the Orisha other then just how it relates in modern day. I'm curious on how it was actually set down and how the religion actually interacted with the people. Just curious since I really have no idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T20:08:38-08:00","id":1270260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270204#post1270204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As how this relate to the Arahamic faiths, well that depends. No one is objecting that If you don't want to play it like that you have to and that's fine anyhow, you do as you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kyman objected to it. This is how this entire discussion started.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T20:18:19-08:00","id":1270262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270209#post1270209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, Scion\u2019s about Myth, not Religion. Worship doesn\u2019t define a \u201cGod\u201d in this context, Legend does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I refused to define &quot;god&quot; when Kyman asked me to, and it was you who brought worship into the conversation. I responded to that and pointed to what yazata<i> means</i> to show a distinction from angels, who were not worshipped. <i>You</i> said that the Tuatha De Danann were not worshipped as gods, so the fact that their name literally refers to them as gods is actually relevant.<br /> <br /> There is no overarching definition of divinity, so you have to use any given culture's definition when discussing their particular gods. I never said worship was necessary to be a god, but the information I have available to me indicates that &quot;was never worshipped&quot; is not something anyone can say with absolute certainty about the figures you named, unless you eliminate the sources you don't like.<br /> <br /> Anyway, given all the shifting of goalposts I'm out of here.<br /> <br /> Treating people like this is not a good look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-25-2018, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T20:48:36-08:00","id":1270264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270262#post1270262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said worship was necessary to be a god, but the information I have available to me indicates that &quot;was never worshipped&quot; is not something anyone can say with absolute certainty about the figures you named, unless you eliminate the sources you don't like. Which is, I guess, a <i>way</i> to do scholarship, but it's not really a good way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... what? You didn't provide any sources for your claim about the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann being worshiped as Gods. I provided a book written by an ex-ASNC Professor from Cambridge and current Professor at Oxford that is literally on the topic, and the most recent scholarly work on the topic as well as being incredibly accessible to a non-scholarly audience. The 'Window to the Iron Age' theory that the idea the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann were worshiped was thrown out in the early 1990s.<br /> <br /> Like, look, I don't want to get into the whole Monotheism discussion because it gets really into semantics, but attacking my approach to scholarship is a wildly low blow mate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T21:08:02-08:00","id":1270267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1270260#post1270260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kyman objected to it. This is how this entire discussion started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't put words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> You noted &quot;At my table, only Actual Gods can have Scions&quot; with the implication that entities serving a higher power that do not consider themselves Gods would not count, specifically the Angels serving YHWH.<br /> <br /> I point out that by this definition, the Orisha (and as another user noted, the Yazata) would not consider themselves Gods. I intended this as a &quot;Honestly what the game considers to be a viable patron may not align with beings that consider themselves Gods&quot;<br /> <br /> To which <i>you</i> replied that the Orisha are definitely Gods, while the Angels would not be. For... REASONS, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I noted that that was a bit presumptuous but did also note that it was &quot;Your table, your rules. Nobody is going to force you to play a certain way&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll bow out of this though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T11:26:19-08:00","id":1270384,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">OK folks, let's get this back on topic and drop the he said/she said stuff. Resplendent Fire that comment about scholarship definitely reads as a cheap shot, not cool or necessary. If I was in your position I would strongly consider posting some kind of apology, or at least PM'ing one to Watcher.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T21:29:58-08:00","id":1274302,"title":"","content":"Have related, but a slight off topic on the subject - <b>How does HISTORY of Scions and Monotheism worked in game world? </b>Did Catholic Church ruled for over one and half millenium on most of Europeans minds? Did Inquisition hunted Scions of 'pagan' gods? In other way stated - <b>Did Monotheism became State Religions on West countries, like in Real Life it went?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2018, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T00:40:12-08:00","id":1274325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274302#post1274302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have related, but a slight off topic on the subject - <b>How does HISTORY of Scions and Monotheism worked in game world? </b>Did Catholic Church ruled for over one and half millenium on most of Europeans minds? Did Inquisition hunted Scions of 'pagan' gods? In other way stated - <b>Did Monotheism became State Religions on West countries, like in Real Life it went?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If we look at the history of the two monotheistic pantheons currently written up for the game, we can see that the history of the Orisha and Deva went largely as it has in our world. The religion of the Orisha is still extant in their ancestral homelands, and the many religions that they've influenced, like Vodoun and Santeria are also likely just as popular in the World as they are in ours, if not more so.<br /> <br /> As for the Deva, we know that they also continue to have large numbers of worshippers in the World, and I don't think any of the polytheistic faiths have made too much of a dent in them.<br /> <br /> Since you mention the Catholic Church I assume you also want to know about the Abrahamic religions? The basic assumption is that they are still the dominant faiths of the Western and middle eastern parts of the World, just not to the same degree as they are in ours.<br /> <br /> Edit: another monotheistic pantheon, the Yazata, are set to appear in Companion... It'll be interesting to see how their history unfolds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 12-14-2018, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T00:43:23-08:00","id":1274326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274302#post1274302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have related, but a slight off topic on the subject - <b>How does HISTORY of Scions and Monotheism worked in game world? </b>Did Catholic Church ruled for over one and half millenium on most of Europeans minds? Did Inquisition hunted Scions of 'pagan' gods? In other way stated - <b>Did Monotheism became State Religions on West countries, like in Real Life it went?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The answer for my table is that history looks largely the same except that the Church pushed the acceptance of Christ without demanding the abandonment of the gods of one\u2019s forefathers. They couldn\u2019t - you demand that and the gods show up and break your windows!<br /> <br /> So Christianity still dominates in the West, and for the bulk of its history oppressed those who wouldn\u2019t accept their doctrine, but it didn\u2019t worry about people ALSO keeping their household shrines, having solstice festivals where pagan gods are invoked, etc etc. But you challenge their doctrine on Christ and salvation, and then the heresy trials start.<br /> <br /> That said, you do get some Christian groups going more extreme - the Puritans for example saw the Protestant reformation as an opportunity to reject Rome\u2019s acceptance of vestigial paganism. But most Protestant Churches (and certainly not the Anglicans) did not follow suit.<br /> <br /> This also neatly means the history of European antisemitism doesn\u2019t really change, since by definition the Jews unlike the pagans could not just add Jesus as Savior to their theology. They\u2019re more true henotheists actively rejecting any worship of pagan gods (though not their existence) in favor of their one true God (or no God, plenty of Jewish antitheists as well). Not being a proslytizing religion, this doesn\u2019t rouse the fury of any Pantheons save possibly the Canaanite Elohim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T11:28:05-08:00","id":1274403,"title":"","content":"But we do not have any canon answer for <b>Scion</b> on 'Christianity oppression', beside the mysterious 'this world works like ours, only some people still worship the religions of their 'pagan' forefather', yes? Nothing directly pointed in books on Christianity versus Gods worshipers conflicts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2018, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T13:29:27-08:00","id":1274440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274403#post1274403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we do not have any canon answer for <b>Scion</b> on 'Christianity oppression', beside the mysterious 'this world works like ours, only some people still worship the religions of their 'pagan' forefather', yes? Nothing directly pointed in books on Christianity versus Gods worshipers conflicts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well from the Orisha, we know that the Atlantic Slave Trade was a thing... And there's passages here and there in the Origin book about how most (presumably) Christian priests would prefer that people not worship other gods but do nothing to stop them. And that many people visit a Church on Sunday and then make offerings in the temple later in the day, and see no contradiction.<br /> <br /> I've no doubt that there were conflicts between the <i><b>Abrahamic</b></i> Faiths and the other Faiths, inasmuch as many religions clashed in the past. I mean, the Nemetondevos are dead, albeit thanks to Caesar and the Theoi rather than any form of Christianity. And it IS official that the Abrahamic faiths are still widespread in the World. It's just that the Faiths of Old that in OUR world were wiped out and in some cases are being reconstructed... Those persisted to a degree in the World.<br /> <br /> But for minor minute details... The details are up to the individual table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T13:35:29-08:00","id":1274444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274403#post1274403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we do not have any canon answer for <b>Scion</b> on 'Christianity oppression', beside the mysterious 'this world works like ours, only some people still worship the religions of their 'pagan' forefather', yes? Nothing directly pointed in books on Christianity versus Gods worshipers conflicts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not printed in canon currently. They don\u2019t delve into rewriting history as of yet since they\u2019re mainly just interested in expanding the World as it is. But if we get some historic setting shards later exploring said conflict would be possible. I think Neall\u2019s mentioned Julian the Hellene/Apostate/Philosopher\u2019s Roman Empire is on the shortlist of alternate settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T15:07:37-08:00","id":1274466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274403#post1274403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we do not have any canon answer for <b>Scion</b> on 'Christianity oppression', beside the mysterious 'this world works like ours, only some people still worship the religions of their 'pagan' forefather', yes? Nothing directly pointed in books on Christianity versus Gods worshipers conflicts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ye, that kind of annoys me too, but as it is a complicated subject, and the point of the game is not a historical one (can be used as, but isnt focused on being) I totally understand why they didnt go for the topic.<br /> .<br /> I think the idea is: the World is our world +. Which means, it is, and was like in our world, except that there were special things and circumstances because of the Gods. So, if you are asking if the Inquisition happen, the answer would be &quot;yes, but with some differences&quot;. Like, it wouldnt go to some places in the world, as Catholicism would be weaker thanks to the influence of the Gods; be even worse (as some of the people on the Inquisition might be Abrahamic Saints or Scions, if those exist); in some places it would end up being an armed conflict, as some Scions would be more hard to capture than others; etc...<br /> <br /> Go for what is more interesting for your game. And dont try to think about it too much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T19:04:13-08:00","id":1274486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274440#post1274440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's passages here and there in the Origin book about how most (presumably) Christian priests would prefer that people not worship other gods but do nothing to stop them. And that many people visit a Church on Sunday and then make offerings in the temple later in the day, and see no contradiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this description give me some image to work with. In a way, it IS similar to our world - remember that, for example, Catholic Church is banning 'magical practices' - and yet still people IRL go on Sunday to church, and later that day visit to banned fortunetaller. <br /> <br /> It seems in Scion this dichotomy is simply MUCH more prevailing - and that each side - Christanity and Gods - can send their Scions if matters goes too bad for their side. However, in grand plan, Christanity won on Roman States Religion in 4th century Anno Domini - and so most of Western world is Christan, with Old Gods cults in society, here and there, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T20:42:20-08:00","id":1274492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274486#post1274486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, this description give me some image to work with. In a way, it IS similar to our world - remember that, for example, Catholic Church is banning 'magical practices' - and yet still people IRL go on Sunday to church, and later that day visit to banned fortunetaller. <br /> <br /> It seems in Scion this dichotomy is simply MUCH more prevailing - and that each side - Christanity and Gods - can send their Scions if matters goes too bad for their side. However, in grand plan, Christanity won on Roman States Religion in 4th century Anno Domini - and so most of Western world is Christan, with Old Gods cults in society, here and there, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes forms of Christianity are still the dominant religion in Europe and the Americas. But thanks to the active Pantheons and their Scions, European pagan cults never died out completely (to be later reconstructed) like in our reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T02:16:42-08:00","id":1274679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274486#post1274486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems in Scion this dichotomy is simply MUCH more prevailing - and that each side - Christanity and Gods - can send their Scions if matters goes too bad for their side. However, in grand plan, Christanity won on Roman States Religion in 4th century Anno Domini - and so most of Western world is Christan, with Old Gods cults in society, here and there, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>See y'all're making a bold assumption there.<br /> <br /> An assumption that YHWH and the Angelic Host is less real than the other religions. At my Table, I've actually had moments implying that the Christian God is just as active as any other Primordial-tier God in the World.<br /> <br /> BIG, and often acts through intermediaries because of that bigness. But some people will get omens and signs from YHWH as much as they might get signs from Odin or from Hermes.<br /> <br /> And I often see people ask &quot;Wait how did the banner of Christianity spread when faced with actual real Gods and their champions?&quot;<br /> <br /> To which my answer is &quot;Why do you assume the other side didn't have their OWN divine backing?&quot;<br /> <br /> Neall has said in other materials that he doesn't want to make people feel like they've picked 'wrong' religions. There's no OFFICIAL Abrahamic Pantheon because <i>hoooo-NELLY</i> that is a potential minefield of awkward. But! I don't take this to mean the same thing as &quot;The God of Abraham worshiped by the Christians, Muslims, and Jewish people to some degree doesn't exist in the World&quot;. Just &quot;Yes, this exists... <b>We are not touching that with a ten foot pole</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yes, as Glamourweaver notes... The Abrahamic Faiths may have tried, but they didn't <i>quite</i> manage to crush the other religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T03:35:15-08:00","id":1274681,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that wyrdhamster was making that assumption; but yes. One reason why I like the several fan efforts to construct Abrahamic Pantheons is that actually <i>playing</i> a Christian Saint or Scion or even an angel in a sufficiently high-powered game actually appeals to me; and I can't do that without an Abrahamic Pantheon to work with. So seeing people put in the effort to construct such a Pantheon in a manner that's consistent with the rest of Scion and without framing them as \u201cthe bad guys\u201d is very encouraging. <br /> <br /> And in that regard, it's worth repeating that Judaism doesn't have the same proselytizing nature of Christianity and Islam: there was a time when Judaism was in active conflict with more traditional Scion Pantheons, mostly surrounding the founding and continuing existence of the original Israeli state; but even then, they were arguably no more oppressive than the religions of the neighboring kingdoms they were at war with. <br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that early Christianity in particular wasn't about oppressing other Pantheons and in fact went through its first several centuries <i>being</i> oppressed (by the Theoi, mainly); and even to this day, there are significant sects of Christianity who believe that conversion cannot be forced, and so tolerate adherents of other faiths: in the world of Scion, I see such sects being even more prominent within Christianity than they are in the real world. Yes, there are conflicts between the Abrahamic Pantheon and the official Pantheons; but they're arguably no more severe than the conflicts among the official Pantheons. And being the top dog in much of human society does not automatically make you the oppressor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T15:34:19-08:00","id":1274790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274681#post1274681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but they're arguably no more severe than the conflicts among the official Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like, the Theoi helped destroy the Nemetondevos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T18:07:23-08:00","id":1274813,"title":"","content":"It how the Shen(?) are the result of one Pantheon conquering and subsuming several others, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T05:21:34-08:00","id":1274868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274681#post1274681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that wyrdhamster was making that assumption; but yes. One reason why I like the several fan efforts to construct Abrahamic Pantheons is that actually <i>playing</i> a Christian Saint or Scion or even an angel in a sufficiently high-powered game actually appeals to me; and I can't do that without an Abrahamic Pantheon to work with. So seeing people put in the effort to construct such a Pantheon in a manner that's consistent with the rest of Scion and without framing them as \u201cthe bad guys\u201d is very encouraging.<br /> <br /> And in that regard, it's worth repeating that Judaism doesn't have the same proselytizing nature of Christianity and Islam: there was a time when Judaism was in active conflict with more traditional Scion Pantheons, mostly surrounding the founding and continuing existence of the original Israeli state; but even then, they were arguably no more oppressive than the religions of the neighboring kingdoms they were at war with.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that early Christianity in particular wasn't about oppressing other Pantheons and in fact went through its first several centuries <i>being</i> oppressed (by the Theoi, mainly); and even to this day, there are significant sects of Christianity who believe that conversion cannot be forced, and so tolerate adherents of other faiths: in the world of Scion, I see such sects being even more prominent within Christianity than they are in the real world. Yes, there are conflicts between the Abrahamic Pantheon and the official Pantheons; but they're arguably no more severe than the conflicts among the official Pantheons. And being the top dog in much of human society does not automatically make you the oppressor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's also worth noting that in our world Christianity made many of its inroads by strongly associating its saints and angels with the gods and heroes of other pantheons. Conversion was high on the list of priorities, but stamping out traditions and stories (often) wasn't. In the World this would be more pronounced, leading to the kind of attitudes we see described in Origin and Hero. In addition, more than a few Theoi, Aesir, and Deva could have mantles in the Abrahamic pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T08:11:58-08:00","id":1274889,"title":"","content":"I would not downplay the degree to which Judaism was anti-pagan, because it was extreme in practice - the Talmud is pretty clear on that - but it certainly would be no more or less vicious than, say, the Yazatas and the Devas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T14:44:46-08:00","id":1274957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274889#post1274889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not downplay the degree to which Judaism was anti-pagan, because it was extreme in practice - the Talmud is pretty clear on that - but it certainly would be no more or less vicious than, say, the Yazatas and the Devas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but being a non-proslytizing faith to outsiders goes a long way to prevent constant pantheon conflict as long as no pagans try to forcibly impose their religion on the Jewish people.<br /> <br /> Christianity and Islam on the other hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T22:47:49-08:00","id":1275027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274957#post1274957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but being a non-proslytizing faith to outsiders goes a long way to prevent constant pantheon conflict as long as no pagans try to forcibly impose their religion on the Jewish people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original citizens of Jericho might disagree. More generally, when Joshua lead the Israelites into their Promised Land, the non-proselytizing nature of Judaism didn't matter much to the locals. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1274957#post1274957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christianity and Islam on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026aren't always about forced conversion. I can only really speak about Christianity in this regard, as I don't know much about Islam; but as I said in my previous post, there are large segments of the Christian community who are big on sharing the Gospel message with others, but who insist that conversion must not be coerced \u2014 and in fact that a conversion doesn't really count if it wasn't voluntary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T23:13:25-08:00","id":1275031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1264948-scion-and-monotheism?p=1275027#post1275027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original citizens of Jericho might disagree. More generally, when Joshua lead the Israelites into their Promised Land, the non-proselytizing nature of Judaism didn't matter much to the locals. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered caveating about the Canaanite Pantheon, but I assumed we all were on the same page that we were talking about the Abrahamic religions as they interact with the World today, so a counter example you\u2019d have to go back 3,000 years for seemed unnecessary.<br /> <br /> As to the Christianity and Islam not always being forced conversions - I didn\u2019t say they were. I said they\u2019re proselytizing faiths (unlike Judaism) which is going to create inter-Pantheon conflict as gods don\u2019t tend to like people telling their worshipers they shouldn\u2019t worship them.<br /> <br /> Buddhism of course is also a proslytizing faith, and does have cases of coming into conflict with pantheons, but compared to the Abrahamic religions is much more adaptable around existing beliefs about the divine (the Shen and the Kami being obvious examples of pantheons who have accommodated Buddhism well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-18-2018, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}